WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.460
Strange days we're living in.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:52.170
To think I'm taking a high and mighty Melkian
officer up to the front lines for an inspection.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.880
This is business. Nothing special about it.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.170
Here, have a seat.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.630
We just got a report in!

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.040
EX-10 and Niitan are under attack
by a large Veela force!

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:26.670
For how long?

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.670
It started about an hour ago.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:31.000
The casualty reports are still unconfirmed.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.420
That was fast.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.380
Right after the Melkia-Kummen
alliance was signed.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.080
Do we move out or...?

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.880
What do you think, Captain Rochina?

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:46.420
I doubt the smell of gunsmoke
would offend a man like you.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.710
All I want... is to see Chirico again.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:01.630
Intentions

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:23.080
Burn every nook and cranny!
Drive those Veela out!

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:26.830
Captain, it's been a half hour since
the shooting stopped north of the base.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.960
We can't find any of them to the east!

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.540
Keep looking!

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.170
Captain, they aren't here!

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.790
That's impossible!

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.710
Sir, this was a decoy operation!

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.250
We have to get to Niitan and defend it!

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.500
And what if they destroy the base when we do?

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.710
Are you going to take responsibility for that?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.130
Well, are you?

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:30.920
Come on, dammit! Turn over!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.580
Oh, shit!

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:42.000
Vanilla, here!

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.830
Son of a...!

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.380
Vanilla, look out!

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.380
My feathers! My feathers!

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.250
Turn around, you idiot!

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.210
Oh, that feels good!

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.630
The curtains! The curtains!

00:05:06.500 --> 00:05:09.080
Vanilla, this is hopeless. We have to run!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.290
Just run and lose the club?

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:14.250
We don't have any choice!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.000
They'll be here any minute!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Look!

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.710
I'm not moving from this spot!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.250
You stubborn...!

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:26.830
I said I'm not moving!

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.040
Let's go!

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.040
I'm worried about my friends.
Take care of this!

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:04.630
Careful! There're Veela all over the place!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.750
I hear you!

00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:26.580
Vanilla, come on! Come on!

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:29.420
If you wanna run, then go by yourself!

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:31.630
I'm not going to let you die!

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.080
Who's gonna die?!

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.420
Let go of me! Coconna!

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:54.000
My club!

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:02.380
Help's here!

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.080
Chirico! You all right?

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.290
Yeah, but the club's burned to the ground.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:34.540
God dammit! Now where am I
gonna buy a decent drink?

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:04.880
Where are you? Where are you, Ypsilon?

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:15.500
Ninety percent of Niitan has been
burned to the ground.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:19.750
Government, police, and
defense force buildings are destroyed.

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:20.920
Communications have been cut.

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:22.080
And the Assemble base?

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:22.960
Unconfirmed.

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:26.380
A small number of ATs are engaging our forces.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:28.670
This is a major victory!

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:33.830
Without the food Niitan supplied to the base
the Assemble isn't long for this world.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.330
Excellent. Now recall our forces.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:38.380
Recall...?!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:39.500
Sir, I protest!

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:44.710
They have most of their forces
rushing to the scene.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:47.000
I know Chirico is with them!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.750
Highness, give me the order to join the battle!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.210
This battle isn't simply for your benefit.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:57.830
An hour's victory isn't worth the loss of more men.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.210
Recall them.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.380
Then when do I go out?

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:03.460
Calm yourself, man!

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.040
You're taking this rather calmly.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:17.540
Don't you think they should send us out?

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.750
Or are you thinking of him?

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:24.290
No.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.920
Well then, what's wrong?

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:31.460
I'm... afraid to fight.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.130
Th-that's impossible!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.960
We Perfect Soldiers
weren't born to think like that!

00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:39.380
I don't know why.

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.630
But I'm afraid!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:43.540
I'm afraid...

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.580
I'm afraid of battle!

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:59.500
Monica, are you somewhere on this battlefield?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.170
Right... Just like that... Just like that.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:10.420
Gotcha!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.130
Monica, they've called a retreat!

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.540
That can't be right! We're beating them!

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.750
It's an order!

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:25.790
All right.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.540
What's happening? The Veela are running!

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.670
You're kidding!

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.080
Same here!

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:43.380
It's Kan Yu.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:47.330
That idiot! Now he figures it out!

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.710
Does it hurt?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.500
I'm fine.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.380
Hey, come on.
We came out of that sea of fire alive.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:49.630
Sure the club burned down,
but we can always just build another one!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:50.750
Again...

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:54.580
and again... I keep starting over all the time.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.420
But this time...

00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:59.500
this time I'm getting a job that means something.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:01.830
So, you mean-

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.000
I was wrong!

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:04.880
About what?

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:08.500
I was wrong... about a lot of things.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.880
Cheer up! This isn't like you!

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:13.500
Sorry, sorry!

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.960
Why do you stay with me?

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.500
It isn't so I'll pay you for
bandaging my wounds, is it?

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.670
For once, could you not be so suspicious?

00:12:22.670 --> 00:12:24.290
Vanilla! Coconna!

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.380
Pops!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.710
I finally found you.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:29.960
Where have you been?

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:32.250
Please, I was worried about you two.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:35.040
When I got back from Zaiden
I saw all this had happened.

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.830
By the way, are you all right?

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.380
Yeah, I guess so.

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.040
Business was blazing last night!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.500
It'll be all right. Come to my office.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.000
Not so rough!

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.420
Sorry about that. I'm worried about Chirico.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.460
About Chirico?

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.790
What's wrong with him?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:53.960
Gon Nu went and brought
a real bastard back to the base.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.960
"A real bastard"?

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.500
We brought Chirico, sir.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.670
Send him in, but wait out there.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:12.540
Yes, sir.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:22.750
Kan Yu tells me you disobeyed orders.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:23.580
Yes, sir.

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:28.080
Do you have anything to say?

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:28.960
No, sir.

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.500
Very well. My decision is to
dismiss these charges.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.080
But, sir...!

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:38.250
I've gotten a few complaints
about you from others.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.670
A lack of trust from your men
due to command incompetence!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:45.710
Chirico! What can you tell me
about these charges?

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:50.920
The captain put the defense of
the base before all else.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.380
Is that all?

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:56.380
Yes, sir.

00:13:57.630 --> 00:13:59.790
You've got a good man serving with you, Kan Yu.

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:00.920
You're dismissed!

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.460
Excuse me, sir!

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:13.380
Now then, I have someone here
who wants to see you.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:20.880
You!

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.500
You remember me. It's good to see you again.

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.500
Surprised?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:30.210
You wouldn't believe the connections I have.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:33.330
And it's a small world.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:36.670
Especially for a man who can
only live in a war zone.

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:38.460
Finding you wasn't terribly difficult.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:44.880
When you came here, Captain Rochina
contacted us and told me all about you.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.960
I thought something was going on.

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:49.380
Is the Prototype well?

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:52.210
Yes.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:57.330
Anyway, I haven't paid you this call to repeat
that useless interrogation we tried before.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.380
Quite the opposite.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.000
You see...

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.750
while we have different objectives,

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.920
I propose that we three pool our talent
to retrieve the Perfect Soldier.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.630
For this reason, I'm willing to tell you everything.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.460
Nothing unusual.

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:27.000
Blood pressure and pulse are normal.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:28.790
Neuro functions are normal.

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:31.500
She said she's afraid to fight.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.290
I thought that was impossible.

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.330
Well, she's...

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.000
Why? It's impossible!

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:39.460
There was an accident, you see.

00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:41.130
Accident?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:49.330
You Perfect Soldiers aren't born very easily.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:53.540
During the complex programming
process, a random...

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:56.130
a trifling accident occurred.

00:15:57.130 --> 00:16:00.540
All because of that, the problem began.

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:03.080
What was it? Tell me!

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.080
When she was born, the first thing she saw...

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:08.040
was Chirico.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:11.830
The PS Project began when we gathered

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:16.630
experts in the fields of genetics,
biology, and neuroscience.

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:21.500
Their goal was clearly stated:
create a perfect warrior.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:23.210
Perfect in what way?

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.750
Microcomputer systems integrated into its body.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.330
Precision mental functions.

00:16:27.330 --> 00:16:30.540
Offensive capabilities equal to
several normal men.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:37.580
As you already know, the reflex mechanism of
a normal human isn't nearly so well-developed.

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.830
The Perfect Soldier is adapted to this age.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:43.250
Literally, a new type of human.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:49.630
It has a more developed
neuro-muscular structure than normal.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.750
Using the latest scientific techniques,

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:59.670
we reconstructed its body systems
to an extremely high level.

00:16:59.670 --> 00:17:02.920
This was made possible by genetic manipulation.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:10.750
In the second stage we encountered an obstacle.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:15.210
How to integrate combat data into the mind
as instinctive knowledge.

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:21.130
All mental processes in an
adult PS are suspended

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:24.460
and combat knowledge is programmed into it.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.080
All its first memories are
fixed into its subconscious

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:31.330
which vastly increases its
learning speed and retention.

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:32.330
I see.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:37.250
Of course, once that's done,
anyone can load it with any data.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:41.580
Twenty hours are required
to completely program it.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:45.040
You mean, after that, it's just like one of us?

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:48.920
Exactly. The PS is born with a body
like a regular person's.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.460
After one month, you can't tell it
from a normal human.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.290
The Prototype was asleep inside that container

00:17:54.290 --> 00:17:57.790
on the asteroid base you attacked,
awaiting its programming.

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:01.500
After it was stolen and
programmed by that secret society,

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:03.500
we suspended our own research.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:07.920
And now there's another PS.
The one called Ypsilon.

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:12.630
Exactly, Chirico.

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:14.880
So, will you help us?

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.630
Why me?

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.330
You're the only man who's
proven a match for them.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.580
You'll be compensated, of course.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.830
Before I agree, I want to ask you one thing.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.460
What if she were to see something
before being programmed?

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:33.960
Are you telling me...?

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:35.880
Yeah.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.750
You actually joined up with Rochina?

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:56.750
I'll be safe until we steal the PS back.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.880
I'd better start looking for a new job.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:02.750
The war's still on. I'm sure you'll do fine.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.790
Nah, it's over.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:08.130
Melkia and Kummen are allies now.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.170
They'll be finishing off those Veela in no time.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:16.000
Now's the time for the mercenaries to live it up.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:22.380
It's not just me.
Everyone here will have to find a new job.

00:19:31.540 --> 00:19:34.920
What's wrong? You haven't drank a drop.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:36.920
You're acting weird.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.250
Was the club burning down that big a shock?

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.130
Shut up!

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:45.420
Where are you going?

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:46.670
I'm enlisting.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.040
You're what?

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:51.960
You were the one who said
I had to start over, right?

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:53.630
Well, yeah, but...

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.920
I'm tired of being a parasite in the war.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:00.500
Better to be a hunk of rotting meat
than a nobody.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.920
If I survive, then I'll have done a job
that means something!

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.210
Wait! I'm coming, too!

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:37.130
Here's hoping for success.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.880
All our mercs are being sent out.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.000
I hope we're alive when this is all over.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.000
The Melkian army will gladly assist you.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:48.710
Goodbye.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.960
Come on, why do you want to go with Chirico?

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:16.250
I said I was enlisting!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.000
And I'm sticking with him!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.790
Quit standing there and get on board!

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.330
All right, move out!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.380
Chirico, wait!

00:21:44.250 --> 00:21:45.880
Take me with you!

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:48.580
Chirico!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.250
Take me with you!

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:04.830
It's okay, baby

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:08.960
I guess I'm just used to it now

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:13.210
You never seem to say much

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:17.670
But we have time till dawn

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:24.130
You're just too blunt

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:28.630
Although that adds a little color to you

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:32.960
So long, baby

00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:36.040
I loved you once upon a time

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:40.330
I loved you once upon a time

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.880
Destiny, bonds, realationships.

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:03.460
So human, and yet such echoes of
humanity are out of character.

00:23:04.000 --> 00:23:07.920
Led by the smell of gunpowder,
lit by the fires of Hell,

00:23:07.920 --> 00:23:11.040
they met on a fragment of stardust
in the Astragius Galaxy.

00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:13.830
The first Adam and Eve in six billion years.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:16.580
Was it really a mere coincidence?

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:18.790
Next time, "Fyana"

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:21.960
Trace the path followed
since the shock of that day.

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:24.290
Fyana

00:23:20.250 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
